最优运行点取决于部署特定的因素。通信成本（带宽、能耗）倾向于更大的 \(E\)，而在异构性下的收敛速度则倾向于更小的 \(E\)。实际系统常采用自适应策略：从较小的 \(E\) 起步，随着模型接近收敛、客户端漂移减弱而逐步增大。


当联邦学习在 {#sec-edge-intelligence-federated-learning-work-93a2} 下运行时
联邦学习只有在若干部署条件有利时才能实现实际收敛，这一主题在联邦学习系统的综述与开放问题中得到了强调 (Kairouz 和 McMahan 2021年)：

异构性必须受到足够约束，使得客户端漂移不会主导训练时间。当人群高度异构时，将客户端聚类为更同质的组，或采用个性化方法，可能优于单一全局模型。
客户端参与率必须足够高，以提供稳定的聚合更新。极低的参与率会使梯度估计产生噪声，并加剧选择偏差。
每个参与客户端都需要足够的本地数据以完成有意义的更新计算。极小的本地批次可能贡献高方差更新，从而 destabilize 训练。

当这些条件被违反时，就必须采用替代方法。严重的异构性提示采用分层联邦学习，进行区域级聚合，或采用无需全局聚合的完全个性化模型。极低的参与率表明需要异步协议，即不要求同步轮次。本地数据极少的客户端则受益于小样本自适应技术，而非基于梯度的训练。
这些数学聚合协议证明了去中心化学习在理论上是可行的。在实验室中，在十个可靠节点上执行联邦平均是轻而易举的；而在一千万部频繁进出蜂窝网络的智能手机上执行它，则是另一个工程问题。稳健的联邦系统必须将算法转化为编排、调度与故障处理机制，并且从一开始就假定客户端不可靠。

Algorithmic Performance Transformations
Fusion, precision engineering, and graph compilation optimize the same dense computation by moving fewer bytes, using narrower formats, or letting compilers reorganize kernels. Algorithmic transformations change the work itself. Speculative decoding attacks the memory-bound decode loop by trying to accept multiple tokens per target-model pass, while MoE attacks dense-model cost by activating only the experts a token needs. Both techniques can improve the iron-law budget, but both can also create new bottlenecks if their extra control logic, communication, or imbalance exceeds the work they remove.

Speculative decoding



Speculative decoding shifts decode toward the compute-bound ridge.

Leviathan, Yaniv, Matan Kalman, 和 Yossi Matias. 2023年. 《Fast Inference from Transformers via Speculative Decoding》. International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML), 19274～86.

Chen, C., S. Borgeaud, G. Irving, J.-B. Lespiau, L. Sifre, 和 J. Jumper. 2023年. 《Accelerating Large Language Model Decoding with Speculative Sampling》. arXiv preprint arXiv:2302.01318.
Speculative decoding is a latency optimization that breaks the sequential bottleneck of autoregressive generation by using a smaller draft model to predict multiple tokens, which are then verified in parallel by the target model (Leviathan 等 2023年; Chen 等 2023年). The performance-engineering relevance is arithmetic intensity: a single target-model forward pass can process \(K\) candidate tokens for roughly the same weight-streaming cost as one token, shifting the decode operating point from the memory-bound slope toward the roofline ridge.
图 11 contrasts the two decode paths: standard decoding advances one token per sequential target-model pass, while speculative decoding lets the draft model propose a block of \(K\) tokens that the target model verifies in a single parallel pass, emitting the accepted prefix together and resampling only at the first rejection.
The transformation is useful only when the draft model is accurate enough and cheap enough. If too many draft tokens are rejected, the target model still loads its weights but accepts little useful work. If the draft model is too expensive, verification becomes compute-bound and erases the bandwidth benefit. Batching changes the calculation as well: at large batch sizes the decode phase is already closer to compute-bound, so the marginal benefit of speculation shrinks. This chapter uses speculative decoding to show how an algorithm can alter the performance equation; 作为服务策略的推测解码 treats it as a serving policy with admission control and service level agreement (SLA) consequences.



